cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this reproduction, evaluation harness or ROS2 port, please cite the FAST-LIVO2 paper; if you use the datasets, cite the dataset owners."
title: "FAST-LIVO2 reproduction: ROS1/ROS2 cross-validated harness (Windows Docker+WSL2 and Ubuntu 22.04)"
abstract: >-
  Reproduction and verification project for FAST-LIVO2. It pins the official
  ROS1 implementation and a community ROS2 (Humble) port, restores official
  parameter semantics in the port, and provides a harness that runs full 1x
  replays, evaluates trajectories against published ground truth, audits every
  reported number, and documents the environment (Docker/Noetic for ROS1,
  Ubuntu 22.04/Humble for ROS2, on Windows+WSL2 or native Linux).
